 "title": "Kill your camera fear in 60 seconds",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator addresses ten common excuses people have for not recording themselves on camera. He debunks each fear and encourages viewers to start recording because the worst case is improving speaking skills and the best case is changing your life.",
 "key_points": [
  "\"I don't know what to say!\": Talk about the one thing you simply cannot shut up about—your passion.",
  "\"I'm not an expert!\": You just have to be one step ahead of the person you want to share the video with.",
  "\"I don't like how I look!\": Stop worrying, you are beautiful and handsome.",
  "\"I have bad angles!\": Everyone has bad angles, even your favorite supermodel. Nobody notices.",
  "\"People are going to judge me!\": People already judge you for everything you do in life, and this changes nothing.",
  "\"I feel so cringe!\": Everyone feels cringe for the first 50 videos; cringe is simply the tax you pay to play.",
  "\"Nobody is going to watch me!\": Then you have nothing to lose. Your first videos are just practice.",
  "\"What if I get hate?\": Hate means you reached someone outside your bubble, and social media works on reactions, so it's a good thing.",
  "\"What are people going to think of me?\": They will think whatever energy you hand them and then forget about it the second they scroll.",
  "\"I don't like the sound of my voice!\": Give it a month, and you won't even hear it anymore, and nobody else will either."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: I would encourage you to try recording yourself! Worst case, you either become a better speaker and gain confidence. Best case, it changes your life. These are some common excuses or fears I hear. We are all human. Nobody is perfect. Not even the faces you see online. Give it a try. #selfimprovement #discipline #philosophy #stoicism #mindset. Transcript: I'm going to kill your fear of being on camera in 60 seconds or less and every single possible excuse you could have for not recording yourself. Let's go. Number one, \"I don't know what to say!\" How about you talk about the one thing that you simply cannot shut up about? Your passion. Two, \"I'm not an expert though!\" Spoiler alert, you don't need to be an expert. You just have to be one step ahead of the person you want to share the video to. Three, \"I don't like how I look!\" Shut up, you're beautiful, you're handsome. Next. Four, \"I have bad angles!\" Spoiler alert again, everyone has bad angles. Your favorite supermodel has bad angles. Nobody notices. Five, \"People are going to judge me!\" People already judge you for everything you do in life and this changes absolutely nothing. Five [unclear], \"I feel so cringe! I feel so cringe!\" Everyone feels cringe for the first 50 videos. Cringe is simply the tax you have to pay in order to play and it's worth it. Pay it. Seven, \"Nobody is going to watch anyways!\" Then you've got nothing to lose. Your first videos are just practice. Remember, nobody remembers the practice. Eight, \"What if I get hate?\" Hate means you reach someone outside of your bubble and social media works on reactions so it's a good thing. Nobody cares about the hate either. Nine, \"What are people going to think of me?\" They're going to think whatever energy you hand them and then they're going to forget about it the second they scroll. Ten, \"I don't like the sound of my voice!\" I didn't either. Nobody does at first. You give it a month, you're not even going to hear it. Nobody else will either. Pretty close. I promise you, nobody's watching you as closely as you think. Just go press record and the worst case, you improve your speaking. Best case, changes your life. Follow for more. I believe in you. Peace. Text on screen: kill your camera fear in 60 seconds (or less), 1) I don't know what to say!, 2) I'm not an expert though!, 3) I don't like how I look!, 4) I have bad angles!, 5) People are going to judge me!, 6) I feel so cringe!, 7) Nobody is going to watch me!, 8) What if I get hate?, 9) What are people going to think of me?, 10) I don't like the sound of my voice!",
